    {
      "dom_id": "step-19883",
      "name": "Example: \n                    Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference",
      "problem": "The polar curve $r=k\\cos\\theta,$ where $k$ is a constant, passes through the point $A$ with Cartesian coordinates $\\left(-\\dfrac72,\\dfrac72\\right).$ What is the value of $k?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the polar coordinates of the point $A.$ The distance from $A$ to the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A$ lies in the second quadrant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(\\frac{7}{2})}| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the polar coordinates of $A$ are $\\left(r, \\theta\\right)=\\left(\\dfrac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}, \\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}\\right).$ \n\nTo find the value of $k$, we substitute the polar coordinates of the point $A$ into the polar equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =k(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ k & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the curve is $r=-7\\cos\\theta,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/8aec18033a85129c44765d2670ebe9c931b0c0186c46b74f9b0ea0ae14028b76.png)",
      "html": "<div id=\"step-19883\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"19883\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"5396\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-19883\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-12\">Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"19883\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            