      "worked_solution": "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a|=|-6|=6$ centered at the point $(-6,0).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-6)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "can_dont_know": false,
      "can_skip": false,
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-q281480",
        "name": "Question 13",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/49238b18533c2ded8180a8532325f14c3b052fb32c58a81892877fba2a4ee054.png)\n\nThe polar equation of the given curve is $r=${{field-1}}.",
        "worked_solution": "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a|=|-6|=6$ centered at the point $(-6,0).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-6)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
