        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/1a5390c0531968e8ef7f3817aa7ceb539ea08633fbfce611736cd3b548c17c1e.png)\n\nThe polar equation of the given curve is $r=${{field-1}}.",
        "worked_solution": "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a|=|-1.5|=1.5$ centered at the point $(0,-1.5).$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1.5)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
