    {
      "key": "step-q17263",
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-q17263",
        "name": "Question 10",
        "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
        "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|\\frac{5}{2}|=\\frac{5}{2}$ centered at the point $(0,2.5),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/8375e6709a6a7f34183b821411aaa251341666f948164d498b012f07af744a45.png)",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
        "fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices": [
              {
                "option": "a",
                "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-17263-a",
                "type": "image",
                "value": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/1bf2d67548ff4fcaa9e209f6b79579d1b5bff5b912a2a6f64d95b509620ab224.png",
                "html": "<img src=\"/graphics/q-17263-a-4\">",
                "source_url": "https://mathacademy.com/graphics/q-17263-a-4",
                "source_urls": [
                  "https://mathacademy.com/graphics/q-17263-a-4"
                ]
              },
              {
                "option": "b",
                "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-17263-b",
                "type": "image",
                "value": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/8375e6709a6a7f34183b821411aaa251341666f948164d498b012f07af744a45.png",
