        "dom_id": "step-q17277",
        "name": "Question 12",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/97b246abafb0152ac4f36d3d71476664cfb687fedaae62fc854aad4113a6b082.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the curve shown above?",
        "worked_solution": "The diagram shows a circle of radius $|a|=|-4.5|=4.5$ centered at the point $(-4.5,0).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4.5)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
