      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The circle has center (-4.5,0) and radius 4.5, so (x+4.5)^2+y^2=4.5^2. Substituting polar coordinates gives r^2=-9r\\cos\\theta, yielding r=-9\\cos\\theta, option c. No Math Academy answer or grade for the current question is captured.",
        "confidence": 1,
        "answers": [
