      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The circle has center (-6,0) and radius 6, so (x+6)^2+y^2=36. Substituting polar coordinates yields r^2=-12r\\cos\\theta, giving r=-12\\cos\\theta. The blank requires only the expression after r=. No Math Academy answer or grade for this question is captured.",
        "confidence": 1,
