    {
      "key": "step-q16470",
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-q16470",
        "name": "Question 14",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/aee2a6a03d8dc10cd56e6e2df279fcf88672d0c83d0ae7abc86a0c8b1a3e434d.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the curve shown above?",
        "worked_solution": "The diagram shows a circle of radius $a=1$ centered at the point $(0,1).$ \n\nIn polar coordinates, the equation of such a circle is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
