      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The circle has center (0,1) and radius 1, so x^2+(y-1)^2=1. Substituting polar coordinates gives r^2=2r\\sin\\theta, yielding r=2\\sin\\theta, option b. No Math Academy answer or grade for the current question is captured.",
