      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The circle has center (0,-1.5) and radius 1.5, so x^2+(y+1.5)^2=2.25. Thus r^2=-3r\\sin\\theta, giving r=-3\\sin\\theta. Enter only the expression after r=. No Math Academy answer or grade for this question is captured.",
