      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Multiplying r=k\\cos\\theta by r gives x^2+y^2=kx. At (-1,1), this becomes 2=-k, so k=-2, option a. No Math Academy answer or grade for the current question is captured.",
        "confidence": 1,
