      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "Multiplying r=k\\cos\\theta by r gives x^2+y^2=kx. At (-1,\\sqrt{3}), this becomes 1+3=-k, so k=-4, option a. No Math Academy answer or grade for the current question is captured.",
