    {
      "key": "step-q281742",
      "question": {
        "dom_id": "step-q281742",
        "name": "Question 20",
        "problem": "If the polar curve $r=k\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ where $k$ is a constant, passes through the point $A$ with Cartesian coordinates $(-3,\\sqrt{3}),$  then $k=${{field-1}}.",
        "worked_solution": "First, we find the polar coordinates of the point $A.$ The distance from $A$ to the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A$ lies in the second quadrant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{-3}| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the polar coordinates of $A$ are $(r,\\theta )=(2\\sqrt{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$ \n\nTo find the value of $k$, we substitute the polar coordinates of the point $A$ into the polar equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =k\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =k(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the curve is $r=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/def95f29f6397b0f6eab20afb6327d8f3f99fdc52fbeac0b0c2af8b228d060a9.png)",
        "calculator_instructions": "",
        "fields": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
            "type": "blank",
            "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
            "tag": "mathquill",
            "choices": [],
            "dom_index": 0,
            "disabled": false,
            "input_html": "<div id=\"freeResponseTextbox-1\" class=\"matheditor-wrapper-answer\" ;=\"\" style=\"min-width:35px;\n                                        margin-left:6px;\n                                        margin-right:1px;\n                                        background:;\"><div class=\"mq-editable-field mq-math-mode\" style=\"border: none; outline: none;\"><span class=\"mq-textarea\"><textarea autocapitalize=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\"true\" style=\"\" disabled=\"\"></textarea></span><span class=\"mq-root-block\" mathquill-block-id=\"33\"><span mathquill-command-id=\"35\" class=\"\">−</span><span mathquill-command-id=\"37\">4</span></span></div></div>",
            "rendered_text": "−4",
